    "review_basis":"The later broad-politic rule supersedes unnecessary fragmentation. From Yellow Turban suppression through his Changsha governorship Sun Jian held Han military/administrative offices; the 190 anti-Dong Zhuo campaign did not create a durable independent Sun Jian polity and remained framed inside the Han political order. Eastern Han is therefore sufficient as the Person-politic context, while serves prevents the imperial territory from being misread as his personal rule."
